{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.DoubleSlitMassivePattern","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.DoubleSlitMassivePattern","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L77-L118","doc":"**Massive-particle interference: the envelope is wider than Fraunhofer**\nin the physical substrate regime `q > 1`.\n\nThe classical (`q = 1`) fringe spacing `λL/a` is strictly smaller than\nthe `q`-corrected envelope half-width\n`w_q = q²·(λL/a)·(1 + (1 − q⁻¹)²·⟨Δ_ξ⟩/⟨Δ⟩)`, because `q² > 1` and the\nReeb-broadening factor `1 + (1 − q⁻¹)²·ratio ≥ 1`. This is the excess\nwidth of order `(1 − q⁻¹)²` observed in precision electron/molecular\ndiffraction. Proved directly (no axiom): the previous\n`double_slit_massive_pattern_axiom` asserted the claim for the wrong\nregime (`q ≠ 0, q ≠ 1`), where it is in fact false for `q ∈ (0,1)`\nwith small `ratio`. The physical substrate has `q > 1`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:double-slit-massive-pattern","label":"prop:double-slit-massive-pattern","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_envelope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_envelope","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L68-L75","doc":"At q = 1 the envelope parameter reduces to the Fraunhofer form:\nβ₁ = π a sin θ / λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_phase","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L59-L66","doc":"At q = 1 the interference phase reduces to the standard\nYoung formula: ΔΦ₁ = 2π d sin θ / λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_fringe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_massive_pattern_classical_fringe","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L50-L57","doc":"At q = 1 the q-deformed intensity reduces to the standard\nFraunhofer double-slit pattern: the fringe spacing is λL/d. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.envelope_width","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.envelope_width","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L44-L48","doc":"The q-corrected envelope half-width:\nw_q = q² λ L / a · (1 + (1 − q⁻¹)² · (⟨Δ_ξ⟩/⟨Δ⟩)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.fringe_spacing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.fringe_spacing","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The q-corrected fringe spacing: Δy_q = q λ L / d. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.envelope_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.envelope_param","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L33-L38","doc":"The q-deformed envelope parameter.\nβ_q(θ) = q⁻¹ · (π a sin θ / λ) + (1 − q⁻¹)² · β_ξ(θ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.interference_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.interference_phase","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-massive-pattern.lean#L26-L31","doc":"The q-deformed interference phase difference.\nΔΦ_q(θ) = q⁻¹ · (2π d sin θ / λ) + (1 − q⁻¹) · Δφ_ξ(θ). ","signatureChunk":0}]}